<title>UK: British Steel bags Bulgaria rail order.</title>
<headline>British Steel bags Bulgaria rail order.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Steel said on Monday that it had bagged an order to supply 26,000 tonnes in rail track steel to the Bulgarian State Railways over a period of two and a half years.</p>
<p>In a statement, British Steel said it would help to lay down about 180 miles of rail track in Bulgaria.</p>
<p>British Steel described the value of the order as &quot;multi-million pound&quot; but a company spokesman declined to disclose the value.</p>
<p>&quot;We are deliberately not disclosing the value,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The railway project is being backed by the World Bank.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +0171-542 7717</p>
</text>
